  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Draws and edits Diagrams in the user's diagram editor, a local-first web app running in their browser.\n\nWords: a Diagram is one saved document. A Shape is a rectangle, ellipse or diamond with a Label inside. A Connector joins two Shapes and follows them. A Layout keeps Shapes arranged: a Stack lines them up in a row or column; a Grid has Lanes (swimlanes) crossed by columns, one Shape per cell at most.\n\nTo make a new diagram, call draw_flow with steps and links and let the editor place them. To change one, read_diagram first, then edit_diagram with a batch of edits. After drawing or editing, call screenshot to check the result and fix overlaps or unclear labels. Every edit_diagram call is one undo step for the user.\n\nThe editor must be open in a browser tab; it connects on its own.",
  "durationMs": 6728,
  "stderr": "[diagrams] waiting for editor tabs on ws://127.0.0.1:7350\n"
}
